r sources: `rand` at `rpc.cljc:114-116`,\n   409\t`rand-int` at `jing/dht.cljc:373`; secure generators at\n   410\t`space/dht.cljc:142-151` and `sign.cljc:119-123`; `gensym` at three sites;\n   411\tclocks at `main.cljc:1242-1542` (driver) and `driver.clj:169,206` (JVM lane);\n   412\tambient at `fs.cljc:92,136,271-273`, `repl.cljc:275-277`, `main.cljc`;\n   413\tprinting at `main.cljc` (19) and `antlr/repl.cljc:71`; timers at\n   414\t`async.cljc:52-57`, `storage.cljc:224-227`, `main.cljc:1321,1343`. All are\n   415\tdeferred-scope entries (§9) except the clocks and printing in `main.cljc`\n   416\t(driver). None is in an H0-H4 file.\n   417\t\n   418\t### 3.3 Exempt dialect syntax\n   419\t\n   420\tNot host contact; the H0 gate exempts them by pattern: `catch` type arms;\n   421\t`^long`/`^bytes`/`^String` hints; protocol and interface names in `deftype`\n   422\tbodies and `print-method`; `exists?`; `js-obj`/`(Object.)` opaque sentinels;\n   423\trequire arms whose only purpose is an alias.\n   424\t\n   425\t## 4. The host-implementation contract\n   426\t\n   427\t### 4.1 Stream implementations and their seams (external contact)\n   428\t\n   429\tUnchanged from the tree for sockets (V) and listed for completeness; the\n   430\tstorage, entropy and parser rows are deferred (§9).\n   431\t\n   432\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   433\t| Implementation             | Portable core (V)                          | Seam value a host supplies                            | Status                      |\n   434\t+============================+============================================+=======================================================+=============================+\n   435\t| Ring buffer, memory log,   | `dao.stream.ringbuffer`, `.memory_log`,    | None. (They mint identities today, §3.2: deferred.)   | Existing                    |\n   436\t| remote channel, waitset,   | `.remote_channel`, `.waitset`, `.observe`, |                                                       |                             |\n   437\t| middleware, apply          | `.middleware`, `.apply`                    |                                                       |                             |\n   438\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   439\t| WebSocket                  | `dao.stream.ws`                            | `{:connect! :bind! :unbind!}` (`host.cljc:20-33`)     | Existing                    |\n   440\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   441\t| Datagram and UDP           | `dao.stream.datagram`, `.udp`              | `bind!` (`datagram.cljc:15-23`)                       | Existing                    |\n   442\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   443\t| Durable journal and the    | `dao.stream.journal` over `dao.jing.file`  | Deferred (§9.2)                                       | Deferred                    |\n   444\t| storage beneath it         | and `store.fs`                             |                                                       |                             |\n   445\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   446\t| Entropy                    | Deferred                                   | Deferred (§9.1)                                       | Deferred                    |\n   447\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   448\t| Parser stage               | `yang.python.antlr.*`                      | Deferred (§9.3)                                       | Deferred                    |\n   449\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   450\t| wasm import surface        | `dao.stream.wasm.md` §1                    | The seven imports                                     | Existing spec               |\n   451\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   452\t\n   453\tSeam rule (`abi.md` §6-§7 as acceptance): a seam entry is implementation-\n   454\tprivate, called only by the stream implementation that owns it; it takes\n   455\thost arguments and returns or deposits plain data; it never invokes\n   456\tapplication code; it classifies host errors into data; what it cannot do it\n   457\tanswers as a qualified unsupported outcome. A map of functions that portable\n   458\tapplication code calls to reach the world is a host service and is rejected\n   459\t(`abi.md:143-148`); none exists in H0-H4.\n   460\t\n   461\t### 4.2 The primitive profile: exact manifest (P)\n   462\t\n   463\t`dao.host.*` (OQ2 adopted) is a namespace family whose files contain only\n   464\treader-conditional entries and docstrings stating each entry's law, kind (P\n   465\tpure, M mutating per §2.4) and oracle. Table A is the profile (76 entries);\n   466\ttable B the portable code replacing host libraries; table C the runtime\n   467\tprerequisites.\n   468\t\n   469\t**Table A: profile entries.**\n   470\t\n   471\t+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n   472\t| Namespace          | Entries (consolidated from, V)                                                                       | N   | Slice |\n   473\t+====================+======================================================================================================+=====+=======+\n   474\t| `dao.host.integer` | From `yin.vm.integer.host` (all 25, P): `big-carrier?`, `exact-integer?`, `safe-native?`,            | 28  | H1    |\n   475\t|                    | `host-float?`, `nan-float?`, `infinite-float?`, `promote`, `from-native`, `demote`, `to-native`,     |     |       |\n   476\t|                    | `native->double`, `trunc-native`, `add`, `sub`, `mul`, `quot-trunc`, `rem-trunc`, `compare-big`,     |     |       |\n   477\t|                    | `bit-and-big`, `bit-or-big`, `bit-xor-big`, `shift-left-big`, `shift-right-big`,                     |     |       |\n   478\t|                    | `magnitude-bit-length`, `to-radix-string`; from `cbor.cljc:112-254` (P): `parse-decimal` (digit      |     |       |\n   479\t|                    | string to big, refuses otherwise), `gcd`, `magnitude-bytes` (fresh bytes). `debruijn_code.cljc:315`  |     |       |\n   480\t|                    | reads `big-carrier?` (H2).                                                                           |     |       |\n   481\t+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n   482\t| `dao.host.float`   | P: `float64->bits` (16 hex, big-endian), `bits->float64`, `finite?`, `integral?`, `fields` (sign,    | 5   | H1    |\n   483\t|                    | biased exponent, fraction big) from `cbor.cljc:525-560`, `debruijn.cljc:855-885`,                    |     |       |\n   484\t|                    | `debruijn_code.cljc:232-242` (little-endian hex becomes a portable byte reversal over                |     |       |\n   485\t|                    | `float64->bits`, H2), `data.cljc:77-92`.                                                   