`, `yin.vm.values`, `yin.vm.engine`, `yin.vm`, `yin.vm.debruijn`,\n   549\t`yin.vm.debruijn-code`, `dao.stream.chunks`, `dao.jing.dht`, `yin.vm.linker`,\n   550\t`yin.vm.linker.sign`, `dao.stream.datagram`, `dao.stream.base64`, and the\n   551\tthree Python integer tests.\n   552\t\n   553\t### 4.3 Oracle coverage matrix (table D)\n   554\t\n   555\tEntry to exact file and case. V = the case exists today and exercises the\n   556\tbehaviour through its present namespace; P = proposed, written in the slice\n   557\tnamed. After H1 every V case is additionally run against `dao.host.*`\n   558\tdirectly by `dao.host.conformance-test` (P), which requires the new\n   559\tnamespaces and re-asserts each row below through them (review A6).\n   560\t\n   561\t+---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n   562\t| Entries                         | File and case                                                                                           | V/P |\n   563\t+=================================+=========================================================================================================+=====+\n   564\t| integer: carriers, promote,     | `test/yin/vm/integer_test.cljc` (25 deftests): `carrier-boundary-test`, `compare-test`,                 | V   |\n   565\t| demote, add, sub, mul, quot,    | `division-test`, `bits-test`, `pow-test`, `parse-format-test`, `digit-limit-test`, `bit-limit-test`,    |     |\n   566\t| rem, compare, bit ops, shifts,  | `fast-path-edge- test`, `fast-path-respects-the-bit-limit-test`, `integer?-test`,                       |     |\n   567\t| bit length, radix               | `kind-of-and-number?-test`; `integer_v3_fixtures.cljc` (data).                                          |     |\n   568\t|                                 | `test/yang/python/antlr/int_contract_test.cljc`: `integer-rows- recompute-on-this-host`,               