rted as a **direct refusal** (never a substituted character); unpaired-surrogate   |     |\n   595\t|                                 | encode refusal; the decode cases cross-checked against the corpus `invalid-utf8` class; H1. In H3,      |     |\n   596\t|                                 | direct refusal tests on `dao.jing/digest-string` and `sign`'s message assembly (the consumers).         |     |\n   597\t+---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n   598\t| text: `nfc`                     | `test/yin/vm/debruijn_test.cljc` (80 deftests) example cases (V, examples only); `dao.host.text-test`:  | V+P |\n   599\t|                                 | a pinned subset of Unicode 16.0 `NormalizationTest.txt` (every part-1 line plus the Hangul and          |     |\n   600\t|                                 | composition exclusion rows); written in H1.                                                             |     |\n   601\t+---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n   602\t| hash: `blake3-bytes`,           | `test/dao/jing/hash_registry_contract_test.cljc` (15 deftests): `blake3-official-and-utf8-vector-       | V+P |\n   603\t| `sha256-bytes`                  | conformance`, `fixtures-load-and-agree-with-canonical-bytes`, `segment-matches-total-predicate-blake3-  |     |\n   604\t|                                 | and-sha256`; `test/resources/dao/jing/digest-table.edn`; `jing_test.cljc` (39 deftests) address cases.  |     |\n   605\t|                                 | P in H3: NIST SHA-256 short-message vectors in `dao.host.hash-test`.                                    |     |\n   606\t+---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n   607\t| sign: `keypair-from-seed`,      | `test/yin/vm/linker/sign_test.cljc` (4 deftests): `rfc-8032-vectors`, `canonical-envelope-vectors`,     | V   |\n   608\t| `sign`, `verify`                | `tampering-is-bad-proof`, `key-file-validation`; `sign_vectors.edn`.                                    |     |\n   609\t+---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n   610\t| arrays: all twelve              | `test/dao/data/btree_test.cljc`, `btree_transients_test.cljc`, `psset_fixtures.cljc` (V, through the    | V+P |\n   611\t|                                 | tree); P in H2: `asort` stability fixture (equal keys keep input order), `acopy` overlap cases, and     |     |\n   612\t|                                 | **no-partial-write** cases for `acopy` and `aset` with an invalid index or length on all three lanes    |     |\n   613\t|                                 | (the array is identical after the refusal; today JS and Dart can write first, `arrays.cljc:97-105`).    |     |\n   614\t+---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n   615\t| Jing CBOR writer (table B)      | `test/resources/dao/jing/cbor-v1.json` with `cbor-v1.errata.md` preserved; `cbor_fixtures_test.cljc`    | V   |\n   616\t|                                 | (14 deftests), `cbor_conformance_test.cljc` (14): byte-identical production, `documented-skips-match-   |     |\n   617\t|                                 | the-errata-and-leave-no-case-unrun`; `cbor_test.cljc`; `jing_test.cljc`; `file_test.cljc` (17) replay.  |     |\n   618\t+---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n   619\t| base64 (table B)                | `test/dao/stream/base64_test.cljc` (3 deftests, named above).                                           | V   |\n   620\t+---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n   621\t\n   622\t### 4.4 The driver\n   623\t\n   624\tPer host, outside the core: the seam values of §4.1, clock readings as data,\n   625\tstdin/stdout, process exit, ambient facts as data. `yin.repl.main` is that\n   626\ttoday (V). Its deferred duties (entropy deposit, pump cadence) are §9's.\n   627\t\n   628\t### 4.5 Relation to the conformance kit and the wasm surface\n   629\t\n   630\t`yin.vm.engine.md` §E.5 presupposes a correct host value model. H1 supplies\n   631\t`dao.host.conformance-test` (table D through the new namespaces); E.5.2's\n   632\t\"R, owner, seal, profile and manifest addresses bit-identical\" is downstream\n   633\tof it. The stream-implementation suite is deferred (§9.4).\n   634\t\n   635\t## 5. What porting a host consists of (after H0-H4)\n   636\t\n   637\t1. Implement table A (76 functions) and meet table C for the dialect; green\n   638\t   `dao.host.conformance-test`. Hash and signature bind a library compiled\n   639\t   into the same instance.\n   640\t2. Load the adopted closure with a reader feature only where §3.3 syntax\n   641\t   requires it; the H0 gate proves zero source edits outside `dao.host.*`\n   642\t   and the §9 deferred files.\n   643\t3. The deferred seams (§9) remain per-host work until their design lands;\n   644\t   until then a port supplies them as today's hosts do, by reader arms in\n   645\t   the deferred files, which H0's allowlist permits.\n   646\t\n   647\t## 6. Verifiability\n   648\t\n   649\tByte-level oracles exist for every hot primitive (table D). H0's gate has\n   650\ttwo lists (files permitted non-exempt arms, §8.2; resolved effect calls\n   651\tpermitted) and two negative tests; it scans recursively and treats reading\n   652\tzero files as a failure distinct from zero matches, as do the H2 and H3\n   653\tgrep gates (status 1 is no match, status 2 is a scan error). Every H1-H4\n   654\tacceptance is byte-identical against a named corpus with errata preserved;\n   655\tthe three behaviour changes (§10) each have a direct test.\n   656\t\n   657\t## 7. Consequence for wasm\n   658\t\n   659\tPrimitives execute in-instance. The import module `dao.stream` has exactly\n   660\tthe seven names of `dao.stream.wasm.md:38-46` (V); a primitive import is a\n   661\tboundary crossing and a violation of §2.2 whatever its purity. The gate that\n   662\tasserts a binary's import list is part of the deferred conformance suite\n   663\t(§9.4); until then the rule is stated here and checked by review.\n   664\t\n   665\t## 8. Slices H0-H4 (commissionable)\n   666\t\n   667\tExpand, migrate, contract. Each slice lands alone under the quick tier on\n   668\tthree lanes with recorded test and assertion counts; \"unchanged\" means equal\n   669\tcounts plus any added test named. The slow tier runs once after H4.\n   670\t\n   671\t+-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   672\t| Slice | Phase  | Change                                                                         | Falsifiable acceptance                                            |\n   673\t+=======+========+================================================================================+===================================================================+\n   674\t| H0    | freeze | No `src/` change. (a) `dev/host_boundary/closure.clj` (over                    | Gate passes on the current tree; the committed closure output     |\n   675\t|       |        | `clojure.tools.namespace` parsing) and its output                              | lists exactly 142/140/141 files (§3.1) and the slice report       |\n   676\t|       |        | `docs/design/host-boundary/closure-{clj,cljs,cljd}.edn`, each file tagged with | records agreement with an independent traversal; the gate fails   |\n   677\t|       |        | its §3.1 class; (b) the gate test `dao.host.gate-test` over the closure with   | on one injected `#?(:clj` in a file outside list 1 and on one     |\n   678\t|       |        | **list 1** (files permitted non-exempt host arms, §8.2) and **list 2**         | injected `(random-uuid)` outside list 2 (two negative tests), and |\n   679\t|       |        | (resolved effect calls permitted: the §3.2 sites, plus the callers of M        | fails distinctly when it reads zero files (scan failure is not    |\n   680\t|       |        | entries named in §2.4), exempting §3.3 patterns; the gate scans files          | zero matches). Counts recorded.                                   |\n   681\t|       |        | recursively and fails if it read none; (c) per-lane counts; (d) the corpus     |                                                                   |\n   682\t|       |        | hash set.                                                                      |                                                                   |\n   683\t+-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   684\t| H1    | expand | Create `dao.host.integer`, `.float`, `.number`, `.bytes`, `.text` with today's | Green; counts unchanged plus the named new tests; the new tests   |\n   685\t|       |        | arms moved verbatim where the law is today's behaviour, and **with the new     | require and call `dao.host.*` directly; corpus bytes identical;   |\n   686\t|       |        | laws where it is not**: `utf8-encode` refuses an unpaired surrogate (today's   | the P-entry argument-immutability property test and the M-entry   |\n   687\t|       |        | helpers substitute: JVM `getBytes` emits `?`, `goog.crypt` and `dart:convert`  | prevalidation test pass on three lanes; `utf8-encode` direct      |\n   688\t|       |        | emit U+FFFD, `jing.cljc:66,69,71,132-135`, `sign.cljc:62-66`, R for the        | refusal test and `utf8-decode` strict tests pass. List 1 grows by |\n   689\t|       |        | library behaviour); `utf8-decode` is extracted from the already strict         | five files.                                                       |\n   690\t|       |        | `cbor.cljc:1240-1271` (V). The `Float64`/`Rational`/`Decimal` deftypes move    |                                                                   |\n   691\t|       |        | with their protocol blocks. Tests: `dao.host.conformance-test`,                |                                                                   |\n   692\t|       |        | `dao.host.bytes-test`, `dao.host.text-test` (table D). Table C laws written    |                                                                   |\n   693\t|       |        | into the docstrings of `values.cljc` and the moved carriers. No consumer       |                                                                   |\n   694\t|       |        | changes, so no behaviour change is observable yet.                             |                                                                   |\n   695\t+-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   696\t| H2    | migr.  | Every consumer moves: `yin/vm.cljc:32`, `yin/vm/engine.cljc:38`,               | Green; counts unchanged plus the `asort` stability, `acopy`       |\n   697\t|       |        | `yin/vm/values.cljc:30`, `yin/vm/data.cljc:41`, `yin/vm/integer.cljc:101`,     | overlap and `acopy`/`aset` **no-partial-write** tests; corpus     |\n   698\t|       |        | `test/yang/python/antlr/{int_heap,int_literal,int_ops}_test.cljc` (V);         | identical. **Pre-deletion gate**: `grep -rl 'yin\\.vm\\.integer\\.   |\n   699\t|       |        | `dao.jing.cbor` drops `:106-254`, `:342-460`, `:483-632` for `dao.host.*`;     | host' src test` lists exactly                                     |\n   700\t|       |        | `debruijn_code.cljc:232-242,315`, `debruijn.cljc:167,241,310-321,855-885`,     | `src/cljc/yin/vm/integer/host.cljc`. **Post-deletion gate**: the  |\n   701\t|       |        | `chunks`, `jing.dht`, `linker:1232`, `sign:55-66`, `datagram:63-66` read       | same command lists nothing and exits 1 (grep's no-match status),  |\n   702\t|       |        | `bytes`/`text`/`float`; `dao.data.arrays` gains the stable sort and            | which the gate distinguishes from a missing directory (status 2). |\n   703\t|       |        | **prevalidation before any write** in `acopy` on JS and Dart (a behaviour      | `grep -rl 'BigInteger\\|BigDecimal\\|                               |\n   704\t|       |        | change, §2.4); the M-entry callers of §2.4 are audited for the freeze rule.    | clojure\\.lang\\.Ratio\\|java\\.text\\|unorm' src/cljc` lists only     |\n   705\t|       |        | Then `yin.vm.integer.host` deleted.                                            | files under `src/cljc/dao/host/`. `yin.vm.engine` is touched (its |\n   706\t|       |        |                                                                                | require) and pinned by the engine suites. List 1 shrinks by the   |\n   707\t|       |        |                                                                                | migrated files (§8.2).                                            |\n   708\t+-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   709\t| H3    | expand | `dao.host.hash`, `dao.host.sign`; `dao.jing` and `yin.vm.linker.sign` require  | Green; counts unchanged plus `dao.host.hash-test`; every corpus   |\n   710\t|       | +migr. | them (`generate` stays, deferred). The string hash forms and `sign`'s `utf8`   | address identical; `sign_test` 4/4; `base64_test` 3/3 on three    |\n   711\t|       |        | switch to `text/utf8-encode`: a **named behaviour change** for strings with an | lanes; a direct test that `digest-string` and `message` refuse an |\n   712\t|       |        | unpaired surrogate (refusal instead of a substituted byte), recorded in the    | unpaired-surrogate string; `grep -rl 'MessageDigest\\|Blake3\\|     |\n   713\t|       |        | slice report; such strings are already refused by the canonical codec (corpus  | noble\\|blake3_dart\\|package:crypto\\|ed25519_edwards\\|goog.crypt.  |\n   714\t|       |        | `unpaired-surrogate` class), so no persisted address changes. Base64 made      | base64' src/cljc` lists only files under `src/cljc/dao/host/` and |\n   715\t|       |        | portable (table B; a replacement).                                             | `src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc` (`generate`); exit statuses    |\n   716\t|       |        |                                                                                | read as in H2.                                                    |\n   717\t+-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   718\t| H4    | migr.  | Portable Jing CBOR writer over `dao.host.*`; `dao.jing.cbor.boring` and        | Green; `cbor-v1.json` byte-identical on three lanes with the      |\n   719\t|       |        | `dao.jing.cbor.cljd` deleted; Boring stays for `dao.stream.cbor.boring` and    | errata skips unchanged (`documented-skips-match-the-errata-and-   |\n   720\t|       |        | the Dart `cbor` package for `dao.stream.cbor.cljd` (OQ4). A measurement:       | leave-no-case-unrun`); fixtures, DHT and linker image goldens     |\n   721\t|       |        | corpus and one large module image, old writer against new, JVM and Node.       | unchanged; the measurement in the slice report, no threshold      |\n   722\t|       |        |                                                                                | (OQ7). Slow tier once after landing.                              |\n   723\t+-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   724\t\n   725\tDependencies: H0, H1, H2 in order; H3 and H4 after H2, in either order.\n   726\t\n   727\t### 8.2 List 1: the files permitted non-exempt host arms, baseline and final\n   728\t\n   729\tThe gate never promises \"no arms across `src/cljc`\", only \"no non-exempt\n   730\tarms outside list 1\". List 1 is generated at H0 by the gate from the actual\n   731\tclosure (every closure file holding a non-exempt arm, §3.3) and must equal\n   732\tthe **expected baseline** below, by category, with each file's reason; a\n   733\tdifference either way is an H0 finding to resolve before H1.\n   734\t\n   735\t+----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   736\t| Category (reason)          | Files (V, from §1 and the closure)                                                              | After H4                    |\n   737\t+============================+=================================================================================================+=============================+\n   738\t| H1-H4 migration sources    | `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc`, `dao/jing.cljc`, | Removed from list 1 as each |\n   739\t|                            | `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc`, `yin/vm/debruijn.cljc`, `yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc`,                 | slice lands; `sign.cljc`    |\n   740\t|                            | `yin/vm/data.cljc`, `yin/vm/values.cljc` (table C blocks stay, as exempt protocol syntax),      | stays for `generate` only.  |\n   741\t|                            | `dao/stream/chunks.cljc`, `dao/stream/base64.cljc`, `dao/jing/dht.cljc`, `yin/vm/linker.cljc`,  |                             |\n   742\t|                            | `dao/stream/datagram.cljc` (bytes arms only).                                                   |                             |\n   743\t+----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   744\t| Profile (the arms belong   | `dao/host/{integer,float,number,bytes,text,hash,sign}.cljc` (seven, P), `dao/data/arrays.cljc`. | Stay.                       |\n   745\t| here by design)            |                                                                                                 |                             |\n   746\t+----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   747\t| Retained runtime           | `dao/data/btree.cljc` (atomic flag `:102-119`, weak and soft references `:212-245`: substantive | Stay, with the table C      |\n   748\t| prerequisites (table C)    | arms, not protocol syntax, retained by design); `dao/data/btree/storage.cljc` (promise facade,  | reason recorded in the      |\n   749\t|                            | deferred §9.1); `dao/pretty.cljc` (`StringWriter`/pprint, display only, §3.1).                  | gate's list.                |\n   750\t+----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   751\t| Codec-track files          | `dao/stream/ws.cljc`, `transit.cljc`, `cbor.cljc`, `cbor/boring.cljc`, `codec.cljc`,            | Stay; owned by that track;  |\n   752\t| (untouched by this track)  | `remote_channel.cljc`, `ws_project.cljc`, `jing/stream.cljc`.                                   | `codec.cljc:45` after C4.   |\n   753\t+----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   754\t| Seams and driver           | `src/clj`, `src/cljs`, `src/cljd` seam and shadow files (§3.1 lane-specific list);              | Stay.                       |\n   755\t|                            | `yin/repl/main.cljc`, `yin/repl/host.cljc`, `yin/repl/state.cljc`.                              |                             |\n   756\t+----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   757\t| Deferred-scope files (§9)  | `dao/jing/file.cljc`, `dao/space/store/fs.cljc`, `dao/space/store.cljc`,                        | Stay until the deferred     |\n   758\t|                            | `dao/stream/journal/file.cljc`, `dao/jing/content/async.cljc`, `dao/jing/coordinate.cljc`,      | design lands.               |\n   759\t|                            | `dao/space/dht.cljc`, `yin/repl.cljc`, `yang/python/antlr/parser.cljc` and the other            |                             |\n   760\t|                            | `yang/python/antlr/*.cljc` with arms, `dao/stream/udp.cljc`, `dao/stream/journal.cljc`          |                             |\n   761\t|                            | (`locking`), `dao/space/transactor.cljc`, `dao/space/schema.cljc`, `yin/vm/ucf/authority.cljc`  |                             |\n   762\t|                            | (`locking`), and every remaining closure file whose arms are only `catch`/hint/protocol syntax  |                             |\n   763\t|                            | is **not** on list 1 (it is exempt by pattern).                                                 |                             |\n   764\t+----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   765\t\n   766\tThe final list 1 after H4 is the baseline minus the first row (except\n   767\t`sign.cljc`), plus the seven profile files. The H2 and H3 library greps\n   768\t(`grep -rl`, recursive) are consistent with it: the libraries they name\n   769\tappear only under `dao/host/` and, for Ed25519, in `sign.cljc`'s `generate`.\n   770\t\n   771\t### 8.1 File-disjointness from the codec track, including tests (re-checked, V)\n   772\t\n   773\tCodec-track source files (`codec.md` §7.1): `dao/stream/ws.cljc`,\n   774\t`transit.cljc`, `cbor.cljc`, `cbor/boring.cljc`, `codec.cljc`,\n   775\t`remote_channel.cljc`, `jing/stream.cljc`, `data.cljc`, the four ws adapters,\n   776\t`yin/repl/{serve,connect}.cljc`. Codec-track test namespaces (`codec.md`\n   777\t§7.2): the 22 requiring Transit, including `ws_test`, `ws-codec-test`,\n   778\t`remote-route-test`, `loopback-net`, `transit-test`, `dao.stream.cbor-test`,\n   779\t`dao.jing.stream-test`, `yin.repl.main-test`.\n   780\t\n   781\tH0-H4 source files: `dao/host/*` (new), `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc`,\n   782\t`dao/jing/cbor.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc`, `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd`,\n   783\t`dao/jing.cljc`, `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc`, `yin/vm/debruijn.cljc`,\n   784\t`yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc`, `yin/vm/data.cljc`, `yin/vm/values.cljc`,\n   785\t`yin/vm.cljc`, `yin/vm/engine.cljc`, `yin/vm/integer.cljc`,\n   786\t`dao/stream/chunks.cljc`, `dao/stream/base64.cljc`, `dao/jing/dht.cljc`,\n   787\t`yin/vm/linker.cljc`, `dao/stream/datagram.cljc`, `dao/data/arrays.cljc`.\n   788\tH0-H4 test files: `dao/host/*_test` (new), `yin/vm/integer_test`,\n   789\t`yang/python/antlr/{int_heap,int_literal,int_ops}_test`, `dao/jing/cbor_*`,\n   790\t`dao/jing_test`, `yin/vm/linker/sign_test`, `dao/stream/base64_test`,\n   791\t`yin/vm/debruijn_code_test`, `yin/vm/data_test`, `dao/data/btree_*`.\n   792\t\n   793\tIntersection: none, with two recorded deferrals: `dao/stream/codec.cljc:45`\n   794\t(`host-bytes?` over `dao.host.bytes`) after C4, and `dao/stream/cbor/boring.cljc`\n   795\t(the transport writer) is **not** touched by H4. The `dao.stream.cbor-test`\n   796\tand `dao.jing.cbor_test` namespaces are distinct files. The deferred H5\n   797\t(§9.1) would touch `ws.cljc:122`, `ws_test.cljc:11` and\n   798\t`remote_route_test.cljc:24` (V: identity-less ring creation), which is why\n   799\tit is deferred behind the codec track as well as behind its own design.\n   800\t\n   801\tCoordination with a host-lane probe track: its \"narrow source adaptations\"\n   802\t(R: the spike touched `integer/host.cljc`, `jing.cljc`, `cbor.cljc`,\n   803\t`cbor/boring.cljc`) are exactly the H1-H4 files; under OQ3 that work is\n   804\tpaused until H4 lands and needs file-level coordination, not just a rebase.\n   805\t\n   806\t## 9. DEFERRED scope (not commissionable under this document)\n   807\t\n   808\tThe following keep their design intent from r2 but are **not commissionable\n   809\there**. They belong to a separate design, proposed name\n   810\t`docs/design/dao.stream.host-effects.md`, with its own non-Claude review.\n   811\tNothing below is decided; the \"required inputs\" are the findings a\n   812\tsuccessor must answer before slices exist. Slice ids H5-H8 are reserved so\n   813\tno other document's citation moves.\n   814\t\n   815\t### 9.1 Entropy, identities, scheduling, ambient facts, printing (reserved H5)\n   816\t\n   817\tIntent: entropy as data the driver deposits (events in); identities derived\n   818\tfrom drawn bytes and carried in creation specs; the driver owns pumping and\n   819\twake-up; ambient facts and the one core `println` as data; `gensym` with\n   820\thygienic naming. Required inputs (from the r2 review R2, R6 and §3.2):\n   821\t\n   822\t- exclusive allocation and resumable consumption of an entropy stream, given\n   823\t  that cursors are non-destructive (`dao/stream.cljc:159-173`) and\n   824\t  independent readers could reuse bytes; partial batches and loss; blocked\n   825\t  resumption;\n   826\t- bootstrap identities: the entropy stream itself needs an identity before\n   827\t  any byte is drawn;\n   828\t- preserved UUID spelling: `ucf/custody.cljc:50-56` requires the\n   829\t  8-4-4-4-12 lowercase form, so a derived id must keep that grammar;\n   830\t- DHT initialization draws several values synchronously\n   831\t  (`space/dht.cljc:255-269`, R): failure and continuation behaviour;\n   832\t- async completions emitted as data: moving consumer callbacks into a\n   833\t  `step!` does not remove them (R2); the `btree.storage` promise facade and\n   834\t  `content.async` consumers need a data-shaped completion;\n   835\t- the JVM blocking content driver selected at `coordinate.cljc:80`\n   836\t  (`driver.clj:169-206`: clock and sleep) is lane-specific IO inside a\n   837\t  portable composition and needs its own disposition;\n   838\t- the codec-track test edits `ws_test.cljc:11` and `remote_route_test.cljc:24`\n   839\t  and the `ws.cljc:122` site: staged compatibility or an explicit dependency\n   840\t  on C4; a re-estimate of the slice (the r2 estimate of about twenty files\n   841\t  was understated: UCF custody and holder migrations are included);\n   842\t- `gensym` hygiene: compiler counters need hygienic naming, not a reset;\n   843\t  `transact.cljc:35` tempids need separate treatment;\n   844\t- OQ9 (entropy shape: stream versus identity-in-spec with driver-minted\n   845\t  secrets; both avoid core generators, the r2 recommendation overclaimed)\n   846\t  and OQ10 (compiler `gensym`) move to that design.\n   847\t\n   848\t### 9.2 The durable-storage seam (reserved H6)\n   849\t\n   850\tIntent: one seam beneath the journal with enumerated lower operations; the\n   851\tclaim-file algorithm portable; capability map (`lock-kind`,\n   852\t`directory-sync?`, `failure-model`). Required inputs (R5, A7): the atomic\n   853\treplacement at `store/fs.cljc:352-387` renames **before** the directory\n   854\tsync (`:364-370`, `:382-383`, V), so a sync failure can leave the new HEAD\n   855\tvisible; the seam must distinguish pre-rename failure (target unchanged),\n   856\tpost-rename visibility (new HEAD visible, durability uncertain) and sync\n   857\tuncertainty, and test post-rename failure explicitly; short reads, partial\n   858\tappends, acquisition outcomes (`held`/`refused`/`unsupported`), durability\n   859\toutcomes per the declared failure model; `own-pid`, `process-alive?`,\n   860\t`create-exclusive!`, `unlink!`, `canonical-path` for the claim-file lock.\n   861\t\n   862\t### 9.3 The parser stage (reserved H7)\n   863\t\n   864\tIntent: the grammar profile plus host walk as one seam value; a\n   865\tremote-stage test. Required input: the one `println` at\n   866\t`yang/python/antlr/repl.cljc:71` becomes an emitted value.\n   867\t\n   868\t### 9.4 Stream-implementation conformance and the wasm import gate (reserved H8)\n   869\t\n   870\tIntent: the contract's outcome tables through a scripted seam against every\n   871\timplementation; a gate asserting a wasm binary's import list against the\n   872\tseven names. Required input: which implementations declare which outcome\n   873\tsubset (`dao.stream.md`, Surfaces).\n   874\t\n   875\t## 10. Cost and what would reverse this (H0-H4)\n   876\t\n   877\tCost (P, from §1 and §8.1): 20 portable files edited, **7** `dao.host.*`\n   878\tfiles added (five in H1, two in H3), 2 wire-writer files deleted, 1 shim\n   879\tdeleted; **at least 5** test namespaces added (`gate-test` in H0,\n   880\t`conformance-test`, `bytes-test`, `text-test` in H1, `hash-test` in H3),\n   881\tthe 3 Python integer tests and `integer_test` re-pointed; about 10^3 tests\n   882\trerun per lane (R: JVM quick tier about 4,000); about 10^1 rewritten.\n   883\tBase64 and the Jing writer are replacements, not code motion, and are\n   884\taccepted only by their byte oracles. No performance figure is claimed; H4\n   885\tmeasures.\n   886\t\n   887\tRisk, revised (review N4): the laws of §2.4 and table A are **not verbatim\n   888\textraction** in three places, and each is a behaviour change with a direct\n   889\ttest: `acopy` prevalidation on JS and Dart (H2), strict `utf8-encode`\n   890\trefusal where today's helpers substitute (H1 law, H3 consumers), and the\n   891\t`aset` return value kept as Clojure's (no change, stated to avoid a silent\n   892\tone). H1 medium: new namespaces plus two new laws and their property tests.\n   893\tH2 medium: nine consumers, the Jing carrier move, the arrays prevalidation\n   894\tchange and the M-caller audit in one slice; mitigated by the corpus, the\n   895\tpre-deletion grep and splitting the slice per namespace if the report\n   896\tshows drift. H3 low-to-medium: the UTF-8 behaviour change is observable only\n   897\ton unpaired-surrogate strings, which the codec already refuses. H4\n   898\tlow-to-medium: the corpus decides; performance unknown until measured. The\n   899\tClojureDart traps are named in §14.\n   900\t\n   901\tReversal: an owner ruling that reader arms are the intended port mechanism;\n   902\ta measured H4 regression that matters (the portable writer stays as oracle\n   903\tand a host supplies a faster one behind the same profile); owner rejection\n   904\tof §12 (then §2 stands as this document's reading of the existing ABI text).\n   905\t\n   906\t## 11. Decision record\n   907\t\n   908\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n   909\t| Id   | Decision                                                                                                         | Status                       |\n   910\t+======+==================================================================================================================+==============================+\n   911\t| HD1  | The governing test: dao.stream wherever the contact can be an IO action with respect to the world (§2.1-2.3); an | Owner rule (\"test 2          |\n   912\t|      | internal pure, total, synchronous function, or a declared mutation of an owned argument, may be a direct call.   | governs\"); r3 wording needs  |\n   913\t|      |                                                                                                                  | non-Claude sign-off          |\n   914\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n   915\t| HD2  | Internal contacts form the primitive profile: 76 entries (§4.2 table A) with kinds P/M and the §2.4 ownership    | Architect r3; needs sign-off |\n   916\t|      | laws, plus runtime prerequisites (table C); in-instance for wasm (§7).                                           |                              |\n   917\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n   918\t| HD3  | Commissionable scope is §2 plus H0-H4; entropy, scheduling, storage, parser stage and stream conformance are     | Owner, 2026-10-20 (\"yes,     |\n   919\t|      | deferred to a separate design with the §9 required inputs.                                                       | proceed with the split\")     |\n   920\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n   921\t| HD4  | H0 gates both reader arms and resolved effect calls over the committed per-lane closure; list 1 names retained   | Architect r3                 |\n   922\t|      | arms; H2's deletion is gated by an exact one-file grep before and an empty grep after.                           |                              |\n   923\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n   924\t| HD5  | H0-H4 are file-disjoint from the codec track in source and tests, with one deferred one-line edit                | Architect r3                 |\n   925\t|      | (`codec.cljc:45`); host-lane source adaptations in H1-H4 files are paused (OQ3) and need file-level              |                              |\n   926\t|      | coordination.                                                                                                    |                              |\n   927\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n   928\t\n   929\t### 11.1 Owner decisions recorded (2026-10-20)\n   930\t\n   931\tThe owner adopted all six r1 recommendations: \"agree with all of fable's\n   932\trecommendations\"; for OQ5 separately: \"makes sense. i agree with fable's\n   933\trecommendation\"; for the r3 split: \"yes, proceed with the split\".\n   934\t\n   935\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n   936\t| Id   | Decision as adopted                                                                                              | Status                       |\n   937\t+======+==================================================================================================================+==============================+\n   938\t| OQ1  | Scope is the `yin.repl` closure; GUI, graphics and demo namespaces excluded.                                     | Owner, 2026-10-20            |\n   939\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n   940\t| OQ2  | The profile family is `dao.host.*`; `dao.data.arrays` stays in place as a profile member by reference.           | Owner, 2026-10-20            |\n   941\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n   942\t| OQ3  | Arm-adding work in the files H1-H3 touch is paused until phase A lands; boundary-agnostic probes proceed.        | Owner, 2026-10-20            |\n   943\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n   944\t| OQ4  | Boring and the Dart `cbor` package are dropped from the Jing content path only; the transport codec keeps them.  | Owner, 2026-10-20            |\n   945\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n   946\t| OQ5  | Storage is a seam beneath the journal, not a streams-all-the-way-down redesign (now deferred, §9.2).             | Owner, 2026-10-20            |\n   947\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n   948\t| OQ6  | This track has its own orchestrator seat, independent of the codec track and any host-lane track.                | Owner, 2026-10-20            |\n   949\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n   950\t| Spli | Commissionable scope is the rule plus H0-H4; the rest is deferred to a separate design.                          | Owner, 2026-10-20            |\n   951\t| t    |                                                                                                                  |                              |\n   952\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n   953\t\n   954\t## 12. OWNER PROPOSAL: amendment to datom.world.abi.md (not doctrine; not applied)\n   955\t\n   956\tThis section is a proposal for the owner's approval (OQ8). It is **not**\n   957\tverbatim doctrine and nothing in `datom.world.abi.md` or `datom.world.md`\n   958\thas been edited. The owner's quoted words are marked as such; the rest is\n   959\tthe Architect's proposed wording, to be revised by the owner.\n   960\t\n   961\t**12.1 Proposed new §8 of `datom.world.abi.md`, \"The governing test\".**\n   962\t\n   963\t> Owner ruling, 2026-10-20 (verbatim): \"when the host boundary can be an IO\n   964\t> monad then dao.stream is used. If it cannot be a monad than dao.stream\n   965\t> doesnt have to be used\"; and, asked whether same-host-ness or the\n   966\t> IO-action test governs: \"yes, test 2 governs\".\n   967\t>\n   968\t> Proposed wording. The machine is the running instance and the runtime\n   969\t> state it owns; the world is everything else. A host contact uses\n   970\t> `dao.stream` when it can be an IO action with respect to the world: its\n   971\t> result depends on world state; it changes world state; equal calls may\n   972\t> answer differently because of the world; its answer is not available at\n   973\t> return; whether it completes depends on the world; or it runs in another\n   974\t> process, host or trust domain. A same-host effect (a file read, a clock\n   975\t> reading, entropy) is an IO action and so a stream.\n   976\t>\n   977\t> A contact that is a pure, total, synchronous function of the machine's\n   978\t> values, or a declared mutation of a value the caller owns, may be a direct\n   979\t> call. Such contacts are enumerated in a host primitive profile with an\n   980\t> oracle per entry ([dao.stream.host-boundary.md](./dao.stream.host-boundary.md)\n   981\t> §4.2), execute in-instance (for wasm: compiled in, never imported), and\n   982\t> add no contract to `dao.stream`. Reads of owned runtime state (a weak\n   983\t> reference, an atom) are neither IO nor profile entries; they are the\n   984\t> dialect's runtime prerequisites. Linking a library to compute a profile\n   985\t> entry is internal linkage (§5).\n   986\t>\n   987\t> §7's two non-adapters are read under this test: a map of functions that\n   988\t> portable application code calls to reach the world is a host service and\n   989\t> is rejected; a seam a stream implementation calls privately to perform its\n   990\t> own IO is that implementation's adapter and is not.\n   991\t\n   992\t**12.2 Proposed change to `datom.world.md:70`.**\n   993\t\n   994\tToday: \"A host boundary is the dao.stream abstraction boundary;\n   995\timplementations do not add contracts.\"\n   996\t\n   997\tProposed: \"A host boundary that can be an IO action is the dao.stream\n   998\tabstraction boundary; implementations do not add contracts. A pure, total,\n   999\tsynchronous host function is a primitive-profile entry, not a boundary\n  1000\t([datom.world.abi.md](./datom.world.abi.md) §8).\"\n  1001\t\n  1002\t## 13. Open owner decisions\n  1003\t\n  1004\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------+\n  1005\t| Id   | Question                                                                                             | Architect's recommendation (not a decision)        |\n  1006\t+======+======================================================================================================+====================================================+\n  1007\t| OQ7  | H4's measurement: what regression, if any, is acceptable for the portable Jing writer against Boring | Accept any regression under corpus identity; set a |\n  1008\t|      | on the JVM and Node.                                                                                 | bound after H4's numbers exist, not before.        |\n  1009\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------+\n  1010\t| OQ8  | Approve the §12 proposal (the ABI's new §8 and the one-sentence change to `datom.world.md:70`).      | Approve after the owner revises the proposed       |\n  1011\t|      |                                                                                                      | wording; §2 stands either way as this document's   |\n  1012\t|      |                                                                                                      | reading.                                           |\n  1013\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------+\n  1014\t\n  1015\tOQ1-OQ6 are closed (§11.1). OQ9 and OQ10 belong to the deferred design\n  1016\t(§9.1).\n  1017\t\n  1018\t## 14. For a successor orchestrator\n  1019\t\n  1020\tDecided (HD1-HD5, OQ1-OQ6, the split): the rule, the exact profile with\n  1021\townership laws, the H0-H4 sequence and gates, the deferral. Open: OQ7, OQ8;\n  1022\tneither blocks H0-H4.\n  1023\t\n  1024\tStart with **H0**: it changes no source; commit the closure tool\n  1025\t(`dev/host_boundary/closure.clj`, over `clojure.tools.namespace`), its\n  1026\tper-lane output under `docs/design/host-boundary/` tagged by class, and the\n  1027\tgate test; confirm the 142/140/141 totals against an independent traversal\n  1028\tand reconcile list 1 with the §8.2 baseline before H1. Then H1 (new files,\n  1029\ttheir direct tests, and the two new laws: strict `utf8-encode` and M-entry\n  1030\tprevalidation). H2 is the first deletion; its gate is the one-file grep\n  1031\tbefore the deletion commit and the empty grep after, and it carries the\n  1032\t`acopy` prevalidation change and the M-caller audit (§2.4). H3 carries the\n  1033\tnamed UTF-8 behaviour change for its two consumers. H3 and H4 in either\n  1034\torder; slow tier once after H4. Do not start anything in §9; a separate\n  1035\tdesign document and its own non-Claude sign-off come first.\n  1036\t\n  1037\tLanes and gates (`docs/agents/build-n-test.md`): iterate on the JVM lane\n  1038\twith `bb test:sub:clj dao.jing` or `yin.vm` (G0); three-lane subsystem test\n  1039\tat each checkpoint (G1); `bb test:changed` across all three lanes in the\n  1040\tworktree before landing (G2); `bb test` on master after merge (G3). Record\n  1041\tper-lane counts before and after every slice. The Dart lane needs `flutter`\n  1042\ton PATH; a fresh worktree needs `npm ci`. ClojureDart traps for exactly this\n  1043\tkind of file: `:cljd` first in every mixed conditional; a tail-position\n  1044\t`:cljd nil` silently fails; protocol method parameters never `[_ _]`;\n  1045\t`(- 0.0)` is `+0.0`; multi-key `assoc` on nil misbehaves.\n  1046\t\n  1047\tReview requirement: this design and any implementation an orchestrator\n  1048\tderives from it under a Claude model are Claude-authored. **Sign-off on this\n  1049\tfinal text (§2 plus H0-H4) and on each slice must come from a non-Claude\n  1050\tarchitect**; a Claude reviewer may review but may not be the sole sign-off.\n  1051\tThe reviewer checks, in order: that every entry in table A is internal and\n  1052\tpure or declared mutating under §2.4, with the freeze rule's enforceable\n  1053\tobligations (i)-(iv) each backed by a test or an audited list; that H0's\n  1054\tcommitted closure output matches 142/140/141 and list 1 matches the §8.2\n  1055\tbaseline by category; that the two negative tests and the scan-failure test\n  1056\tfail as intended; that H2's grep gates hold before and after the deletion\n  1057\tcommit and the no-partial-write tests exist; that H1-H4 acceptance is\n  1058\tbyte-identical against the named corpus with errata preserved and the three\n  1059\tbehaviour changes are named in slice reports; that no H0-H4 edit touches a\n  1060\tcodec-track source or test file except the recorded `codec.cljc:45` deferral;\n  1061\tthat nothing from §9 is started.\n  1062\t\n  1063\t## Appendix A. Citations opened for this document (2026-10-20, read only)\n  1064\t\n  1065\t+--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1066\t| Cite                                                         | Finding                                                                                          |\n  1067\t+==============================================================+==================================================================================================+\n  1068\t| `docs/design/datom.world.md:16-32,43-48,68-71`               | Axioms; side effects as emissions; the sentence §12.2 proposes to change.                        |\n  1069\t+--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1070\t| `docs/design/datom.world.abi.md:21-24,35-44,47-52,56-64,`    | One ABI; custody; machine-internal work in-instance; the floor and internal linkage; effects     |\n  1071\t| `75-87,94-148`                                               | out, events in; adapter discipline; the two non-adapters.                                        |\n  1072\t+--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1073\t| `docs/design/dao.stream.wasm.md:29-52`                       | Seven imports; primitives have no imports.                                                       |\n  1074\t+--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1075\t| `docs/design/dao.stream.codec.md:140-180,658-780`            | Contract namespace; slice file set; the 22 test namespaces (§8.1).                               |\n  1076\t+--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1077\t| `src/cljc/yin/vm/integer/host.cljc:1-298`                    | 25 public functions; \"depends on nothing\".                                                       |\n  1078\t+--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1079\t| `src/cljc/yin/vm/integer.cljc:1-101`; `yin/vm.cljc:32,929`;  | Consumers of the shim (requires and `big-carrier?` sites).                                       |\n  1080\t| `yin/vm/engine.cljc:38,810`; `yin/vm/values.cljc:30,196`;    |                                                                                                  |\n  1081\t| `yin/vm/data.cljc:41,421,547`; `test/yang/python/antlr/`     |                                                                                                  |\n  1082\t| `{int_heap,int_literal,int_ops}_test.cljc`                   |                                                                                                  |\n  1083\t+--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1084\t| `src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:1-60,95-254,342-460,483-632,`   | Reader; big-integer helpers; carriers with equality and hash; JVM Decimal/Ratio construction and |\n  1085\t| `733-784,1070,1177`                                          | access; byte-ordered sorting.                                                                    |\n  1086\t+----------------------------